# Table §Errors — ONE CELL, ONE MARK LINE.
#
# A second `cell (r,c)` line for the same cell used to parse, and only the
# first line's options were drawn: the blue border below vanished with no
# error. The second line is now the error, as a second `width` line is,
# for a data cell and for a header cell alike. A repeated row highlight
# loses nothing and stays legal.
figdown 0.5 table
table t "T"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| a | b |
| c | d |
cell (1,1) fill=#ff0000
cell (1,1) stroke=#0000ff
cell (h1,2) fill=#eeeeee
cell (h1,2) class=k
cell 2 highlight
cell 2 highlight
class k "key"
